{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1519156802,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDE0ODMyNDU4NDE="},"added":["documentation"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1519156802,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDE0ODMyNDU4NDM="},"added":["UX"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1519161836,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2NzEyNDQ1Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2209#issuecomment-367124457"},"message":"FWIW\nI do not see any relevant explicit write attempt in patool.\nIt installs just fine into virtualenv:\n```\n$\u003e venv/bin/pip install patool\nCollecting patool\n  Using cached patool-1.12-py2.py3-none-any.whl\nInstalling collected packages: patool\nSuccessfully installed patool-1.12\n```\nI am trying to avoid `--user` mode and direct invocation of setup.py install as much as I could afford (actually always)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"8b17f086a94c7f0c9fd7fb93ddad5ce893006113"},"timestamp":1519195376,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2NzIyOTA3Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2209#issuecomment-367229076"},"message":"As root without --user it does not work either. The same problems occurs with python3-openssl, python3-duecredit, libffi-dev, liblzma-dev","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1519219914,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2NzMyNjI3OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2209#issuecomment-367326278"},"message":"Did you try pip install, ideally within a virtualenv? Then you could just alias/symlink to that datalad binary installed within virtualenv and it would use modules installed within virtualenv","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"8b17f086a94c7f0c9fd7fb93ddad5ce893006113"},"timestamp":1519220218,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2NzMyNzc0Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2209#issuecomment-367327743"},"message":"No I didn't. It is running now, and I will not touch it anymore. I had a long fight with our firewall and guesing the right git proxy settings. :)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1519220885,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2NzMzMDg3OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2209#issuecomment-367330879"},"message":"Despite not needed for @cni-md anymore, that's actually a nice trick to remember, @yarikoptic.\nWe should put that somewhere as a fallback solution.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1519222651,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2NzMzOTk1OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2210#issuecomment-367339959"},"message":"So, the issue is happening when the DICOM metadata is dumped into a file.\nThe piece that `utf_8_decode` is choking on, is:\n\n```\n(Pdb) d\n\u003e /usr/local/lib/python2.7/dist-packages/simplejson/__init__.py(278)dump()\n-\u003e for chunk in iterable:\n(Pdb) chunk\nu',\\n\"5.3.0.3\"'\n```\nWhich looks weird indeed. Judging by its value it is coming from DICOM header field \"SoftwareVersions\". The aggregated metadata contains the following for that key:\n\n```\n(Pdb) [x['SoftwareVersions'] for x in obj['dicom']['Series']]\n[['5.3.0', '5.3.0.3'], ['5.3.0', '5.3.0.3'], ['5.3.0', '5.3.0.3'], ['5.3.0', '5.3.0.3'], ['5.3.0', '5.3.0.3'], ['5.3.0', '5.3.0.3'], ['5.3.0', '5.3.0.3'], ['5.3.0', '5.3.0.3'], ['5.3.0', '5.3.0.3'], ['5.3.0', '5.3.0.3'], ['5.3.0', '5.3.0.3'], '5.3.0', ['5.3.0', '5.3.0.3'], ['5.3.0', '5.3.0.3'], ['5.3.0', '5.3.0.3'], ['5.3.0', '5.3.0.3'], ['5.3.0', '5.3.0.3'], ['5.3.0', '5.3.0.3', 'G1619@tzres.dll,-322']]\n```\nATM that's confusing to me, since the last entry is the only nonsense I notice, but doesn't appear to contain the `u',\\n\"5.3.0.3\"'` in question.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1519224002,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2NzM0Njg3Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2210#issuecomment-367346876"},"message":"Hold on.\n\nOn the deepest level, it's\n```\n\u003e /usr/lib/python2.7/encodings/utf_8.py(16)decode()\n-\u003e return codecs.utf_8_decode(input, errors, True)\n(Pdb) input\n'\\xb0G\\x841\\x9f6\\x841\\xa49@tzres.dll,-322'\n```\n(as one would expect from the values above).\n\nSo, I'm posting too fast ... ;-)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1519224156,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2NzM0NzY1OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2210#issuecomment-367347659"},"message":"@mih ,  @cni-md, do you have any idea how something like \"G1619@tzres.dll,-322\" (regardless of encoding) could end up in a DICOM header as \"SoftwareVersion\"?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"8b17f086a94c7f0c9fd7fb93ddad5ce893006113"},"timestamp":1519225751,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2NzM1NjkxNQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2210#issuecomment-367356915"},"message":"grep \"tzres.dll\" *\nÜbereinstimmungen in Binärdatei PSg.1.3.46.670589.11.38317.5.0.7584.2018021408330042001.1\nPhilips MR Imaging DD 005\nI have no clue what are the PSg.* files are used for. Real images starts with MR.*\n\ngdcmdump PSg.... \n(0018,1030) LO [DEFAULT PRESENTATION STATE]                       # 26,1 Protocol Name\n\nNo repetition time, no Echo time.... strange file","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1519227623,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2NzM2NzUyNQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2210#issuecomment-367367525"},"message":"Hm Quick search brought me to http://compgroups.net/comp.protocols.dicom/what-is-psg-file/2211546\n\nThe \"we\" in the answer refers to OFFIS, I guess, which - I conclude - is this one http://dicom.offis.de/software.php.en .\nSince I'm not exactly familiar with the details of scanning and what part of the software stack produces output that we really want to see in the dicom dataset, I don't feel qualified to judge, whether or not this means, we can simply ignore those files.\n\nHowever, while this might be a solution in your case, guarding against that kind of sh** probably is a more general issue.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1519230692,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2NzM4NTYwNg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2210#issuecomment-367385606"},"message":"BTW: Not exactly surprising it works in python 3.\n\nIn python 2 I didn't find a way to deal with that kind of string yet, except using `decode(errors='ignore')`, which prob. would be fine in that case. However, that call comes from within `simplejson.dump`, so we can't pass that one in there. :-/\n\nEdit:\nIt \"works\" in Python 3 means: nothing is choking on that value - it gets written to the metadata.\nOf course it's f** up nevertheless:\n```\ndatalad -f json_pp metadata . --reporton datasets | grep \"tzres.dll\"\n            \"\\u764e\\uffc4\\uffff@tzres.dll,-322\"\n```","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"8b17f086a94c7f0c9fd7fb93ddad5ce893006113"},"timestamp":1519284436,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2NzU5MDc5Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2210#issuecomment-367590796"},"message":"Ok, the PSg file strores only the display parameters on the Philips Scanner. If you reload the the dataset on the scanner you get the same display options (contrast settings, zoom,...) as before. \n\nI am wondering that we got this entry only once. We have 8 runs (localizer, 3x EPI, 3x DTI, fieldmap) but I use an automatic QC pipeline from Philips and this pipeline tend to crash after run 5. I assume this shitty entry is an result of this crash?!\nI will check the other QA Scans.","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1521531173,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDE1MzAyMzM2NDI="},"added":["metadata"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1521531187,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3NDUwMTcyMA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2210#issuecomment-374501720"},"message":"I believe this was fixed.\n\nPlease see #2326 for a related RF.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1521531187,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTUzMDIzMzkwMg=="},"status":2}]}